     "answer": "All three were considered and excluded for different reasons. Trehalose was set aside because it is already a widely studied and heavily engineered compatible solute in synthetic biology, so it offered little novelty or differentiation. Proline was excluded because excessive accumulation is associated with cytotoxic rather than purely protective effects, which is a risk in a system designed to produce protectant continuously on demand. CAPE-derived peptides were deprioritised on timeline: synthesis and characterisation were judged too slow for the project window against faster alternatives.",
