     "answer": "Both pGEM-T Easy, the intermediate that fixed cycle 2, and every Level 1 destination vector carry ampicillin. Carryover donor vector is normally selected away at the transformation step, and with a shared marker it is not, so background colonies survive selection. It was found after the fact, in August. The fix was to amplify the coding sequences with the full BpiI and BsaI tail and clone them directly into the kit's pSTK-0C entry vector, which puts chloramphenicol on the donor and ampicillin on the destination; three Level 0 screens on 14 August came back clean at their expected sizes and three clones from each went to liquid culture. Only the coding sequences not already cloned in cycle 3 were affected.",
