     "answer": "Because with a raw PCR product as the donor, a wrong band can be either a failed assembly or an artefact of the amplification, and four of our six cloning cycles are variations on that one problem. pGEM-T Easy pairs its 3-prime thymidine overhangs with the 3-prime adenosine a non-proofreading polymerase leaves, so each coding sequence could be cloned, screened by colony PCR between the flanking T7 and SP6 promoters, and sequence-confirmed before it ever met BsaI. Seven sets, A to G, were done this way, each with its own expected size, and the chromophore operon set F ran at 1,726 bp on 1 July. The cost was a day of picking, screening and minipreps; what it bought was the end of the cycle 2 ambiguity.",
     "answer_zh": "因為以未純化確認的 PCR 產物當供給 DNA 時，一個錯誤條帶可能是組裝失敗，也可能是擴增產生的假產物，而我們六個選殖循環中有四個都是這同一個問題的變形。pGEM-T Easy 以其 3 端胸腺嘌呤突出端配對非校讀聚合酶留下的 3 端腺嘌呤，所以每個編碼序列都能先被選殖、用兩側的 T7 與 SP6 啟動子做菌落 PCR 篩選，並在接觸 BsaI 之前完成定序確認。共有七組 A 到 G 以此方式完成，各有自己的預期大小，發色團操縱子 F 組在 7 月 1 日跑在 1,726 bp。代價是一天的挑菌、篩選與小量質體製備；換來的是第 2 循環那種模糊性的終結。",
     "cite": [
      "engineering/"
     ],
     "trap": "Adding that a confirming restriction digest was also run at this stage; the page says no digest was run, because band size plus full-length sequencing answered both questions.",
     "trap_zh": "補充說這一階段還做了確認性限制酶切；頁面說沒有做酵素切，因為條帶大小加全長定序已回答了兩個問題。"
