     "answer": "No, and our own page corrects it. A colony PCR band says a template of the right length is present in that colony. It does not say where the construct sits, whether it is intact outside the amplified stretch, or whether the plasmid is carried at all. Engineering marks this as a wording fix rather than a data fix: the bands are real and the sentence claims more than they can. There is a related gap on Parts: the archive nowhere records which cargo-bearing plasmid was in which transformant, so no individual part is marked as being in B. subtilis and the single 41 kDa band on the 24 August blot cannot be assigned to a named part either.",
     "answer_zh": "不能，我們自己的頁面也更正了這一點。菌落 PCR 的條帶只說明該菌落裡存在長度正確的模板。它沒有說構築位於何處、擴增區段以外是否完整，甚至沒有說質體是否真的被帶著。Engineering 把這標為措辭修正而非數據修正：條帶是真的，但那句話主張的超出條帶所能支持的範圍。Parts 頁上有一個相關缺口：檔案庫中沒有任何地方記錄哪一個帶貨物基因的質體在哪一個轉型株裡，所以沒有任何單一部件被標記為已進入枯草桿菌，8 月 24 日那張西方墨點 (Western blot) 上唯一的 41 kDa 條帶也無法歸屬到某個具名部件。",
