     "answer": "In April, before the kit arrived, we built our own Golden Gate shuttle vector by moving a dropout cassette into pNW33N. The kit's own library sheet then described pSTK-EXP-1-sfGFP as pNW33N adapted for STK, which is the same idea already done. Our page records it as the instinct being right and the work turning out redundant. All five constitutive constructs were built in pSTK-EXP1-sfGFP instead, because that plasmid replicates in both E. coli and B. subtilis so the same construct can be screened for expression in E. coli and carried into B. subtilis unchanged.",
