     "answer": "Because the useful dynamic range of a two-component system depends on how much sensor is sitting in the cell, and we had no way to predict which level would work in our hands, so we built CcaS-m3 behind two constitutive promoters of different strength, PliaG and PlepA. Both were sequence-confirmed: assembly B on PliaG, clone B2, colony PCR 24 June and sequenced 3 July, and assembly C on PlepA, clones C6 and C9, colony PCR 22 July and sequenced 24 July. Because both survived, the Level 2 assembly was run twice: ACDI carries the PlepA photoreceptor and ABDI the PliaG one. Until an induction curve exists there is no way to choose between them, so we carried both, and ABDI is the weaker record because its junctions have never been checked all three at once in one gel.",
