     "q_zh": "你們最初的設計是讓基改植物生長促進根圈細菌 (TgPGPR) 住在土壤裡。為什麼後來把菌放進機器裡，而這個改變付出了什麼代價？",
     "answer": "The page gives one reason: control. Once a transgenic organism is released, expression, dose and spread stop being ours to set, and the bacteria produce whether or not the plant is stressed and travel with soil and water. What the team needed from the bacteria was the molecule, not the organism, so the organism went into a machine and only the product goes to the field, turning a release problem into a containment problem. The cost is that the project now owns a hardware stack and a delivery step it did not have before: a reactor, a membrane, sensors, a light path and a bottle.",
     "answer_zh": "該頁給的理由是「控制權」。基改生物一旦釋放，表達量、劑量與擴散就不再由我們決定，細菌不管植物有沒有逆境都會生產，並隨土壤與水移動。團隊真正需要的是分子而不是生物體，因此把菌放進機器、只讓產物進入田間，把「釋放問題」轉成「圍阻 (containment) 問題」。代價是專案從此多了原本沒有的硬體與遞送環節：反應器、膜、感測器、光路與瓶裝劑。",
