     "answer": "Two platings, and we should say so. On 6 June 2 mL of shell-side medium from the prototype I run was spread on LB and grew no colonies, and a later run was plated from both sides and photographed after 24 h at 37 °C. There is one plating per run, no replicate within a run, no recorded incubation time or temperature for the June plate, and no log reduction value anywhere; a poster figure filed under an LRV of 7.5 has no measurement behind it and must not be quoted. Our own pages also give the cell dimension two different ways, and Human Practices records that at the 4 September meeting we presented passive leakage of B. subtilis and protectant through the membrane with no driving force as a major obstacle, which has to be reconciled with the containment claim.",
