     "q_zh": "iGEM 的 OD600 校正標準品是二氧化矽懸浮液。你們用的是二氧化鈦，而且最後完全沒有套用校正轉換。請為這兩個決定辯護。",
     "answer": "TiO₂ was chosen because we had it, it performed nearly the same suspended in 1% SDS, and it was much cheaper, so the SiO₂ calibration was deferred rather than dropped; it is written up as cycle 7 and is still not written. Using culture to calibrate was rejected because it grows, settles and lyses between readings, while an inert particle gives a stable scattering target whose added mass is a common linear ground truth both instruments can be judged against. No transform was applied because fitting our readings to the Bio-Drop would tie them to the reference instrument's own error without improving agreement that is already within a few percent, and the Bio-Drop is the slightly less linear of the two against the mass standard. On that evidence calibration is treated as unnecessary rather than pending.",
     "answer_zh": "選 TiO₂ 是因為手邊就有、懸浮於 1% SDS 時表現幾乎相同，而且便宜得多，所以 SiO₂ 校正是延後而非放棄；它被列為 cycle 7，至今仍未寫出。用培養液校正被否決，因為培養液會生長、沉降並在讀數之間裂解，而惰性顆粒提供穩定的散射標的，其加入質量是兩台儀器都能被獨立評分的共同線性真值。不套用轉換，是因為把我們的讀數擬合到 Bio-Drop 只會把它綁上對照儀器本身的誤差，而一致性已在幾個百分點內；且對質量標準而言 Bio-Drop 還是兩者中線性稍差的一台。依此證據，校正被視為不必要，而非待辦。",
