     "q_zh": "流通槽中的氣泡是你們最大的量測問題。你們本可以改光學、對迴路除氣，或在軟體裡過濾。你們做了什麼？順序如何？",
     "answer": "All of it except changing the optics, and in a traceable order. V1 kept the path flat and horizontal, where a bubble parks in the beam with nowhere to go. V2 stood the path up so buoyancy carries a bubble out along the beam axis. Cycle 4 put the whole body on a printed wedge, so no surface inside the cuvette is horizontal, which the mechanical section says clears almost all bubbles within about a quarter of a second at a 10 degree tilt. The tilt was deliberately put in the wedge rather than in the optics, so the cycle 1 beam geometry stays untouched and the wedge can be reprinted at another angle. At the same time we stopped treating bubbles as purely optical and fitted a dual luer valve with syringes to bleed gas before a run, and in firmware a burst-median rejection filter removes what gets through.",
     "answer_zh": "除了改光學以外全都做了，而且順序可追溯。V1 的光路是水平的，氣泡卡在光束裡無處可去。V2 把光路立起來，讓浮力沿光束軸把氣泡帶走。Cycle 4 把整個本體放在列印的楔形座上，使比色槽內沒有任何水平面；機構章節指出在 10 度傾角下幾乎所有氣泡約 0.25 秒內離開。傾角刻意做在楔形座而非光學件上，以保持 cycle 1 的光束幾何不變，並可用不同角度重印楔形座。同時我們不再把氣泡當純光學問題，加裝雙 luer 閥與針筒在運轉前排氣，固件中則以叢發中位數剔除濾波器處理漏過的氣泡。",
