     "answer": "They compare LEDs against each other and nothing else yet. Every intensity on the page is reported in lux, which is weighted for human vision peaking near 555 nm, so the weighting error differs between the green and red channels, while the dose that matters to the cells is photon flux in µmol m⁻² s⁻¹. The team found this in week 16 and the page states that until the readings are converted the numbers cannot be compared with a published dose, including the 4.66 µmol m⁻² s⁻¹ target. The stated wavelength peaks are the classic CcaS/CcaR values rather than measured on our parts, so they are assumptions until the LEDs are characterised. And matching corrects spread at build time only, not drift as LEDs age or warm up during a long run.",
     "answer_zh": "目前只能彼此比較，別的都不行。該頁所有強度都以 lux 報告，而 lux 是依人眼視覺（峰值約 555 nm）加權的，因此綠光與紅光通道的加權誤差大小不同；對細胞真正重要的劑量是光子通量 (µmol m⁻² s⁻¹)。團隊在第 16 週發現此事，該頁也寫明在讀數換算之前，這些數字無法與任何已發表劑量比較，包括 4.66 µmol m⁻² s⁻¹ 這個目標。所列波長峰值是 CcaS/CcaR 的經典值，而非在我們零件上量測的，因此在 LED 被特性化之前只是假設。配對也只修正製作時的散佈，不修正 LED 老化或長時間運轉升溫造成的漂移。",
