     "answer": "The page says so directly: illuminating a plate of cultures from below with per-well control is the Light Plate Apparatus pattern from the optogenetics literature, and our printed enclosure still carries LPA_Box as its part name because that is where the design started. The biology, the CcaS/CcaR green-red switch, is also from the literature and was not designed here, and the dose target comes from the Castillo-Hair characterisation. What we built on top is the dual-wavelength column layout, the resistance-matched LED selection, and the enclosure and tube holder sized for our tubes and our incubator.",
