     "answer": "We cannot answer the second and third parts. The idea came from Professor Chen 陳文亮, who suggested the ReLeaf database as a platform for organizing experimental data and supporting future optimization, and we recorded that he gave us the idea of selling our data. The plan then says year 3 collects real-time environmental data as a secondary revenue stream, used internally to optimize the product and sold externally for market research and crop-yield improvement, and Sustainability's SDG 10 counts data revenue as part of what subsidises smallholders. No buyer, no price, no data-sharing agreement and no farmer consent mechanism is documented. For farm-level data on identifiable holdings that is a gap we should not be relying on for cross-subsidy.",
     "answer_zh": "第二與第三部分我們答不出來。這個想法來自陳文亮教授，他建議把 ReLeaf 資料庫作為整理實驗資料、支援未來優化的平台，我們也記錄下「賣資料」的點子來自他。計畫接著說第 3 年蒐集即時環境資料作為第二收入來源，內部用於優化產品，外部則售予市場研究與作物產量改善用途；Sustainability 的 SDG 10 也把資料收入算進補貼小農的來源。但沒有買方、沒有價格、沒有資料共享協議、也沒有農民同意機制的紀錄。對於可識別農地的農場級資料來說，這是個缺口，我們不該把交叉補貼建立在上面。",
