     "id": "GT-13",
     "type": "decision",
     "q": "Why control production with light rather than a chemical inducer like IPTG?",
     "q_zh": "為什麼用光來控制生產，而不是像 IPTG 這樣的化學誘導物？",
     "answer": "Because light has no mass in the process. A chemical inducer has to be bought, stored, metered into a sterile vessel and then accounted for in the product stream, and it is a running cost that scales with every batch. Light adds no line into the loop, leaves no residue in the permeate, and can be re-dosed from software without anyone opening the vessel, which is what lets a weather forecast drive production at all: the command path ends at an LED, not at a pump full of inducer. On the cost to the culture, growth rate across the six light arms spans 0.279 to 0.317 per hour, all within one standard error, so green induction carries no measurable growth penalty at those intensities. That growth figure is the one whose strain label is disputed, so quote it as growth only.",
     "answer_zh": "因為光在製程裡沒有質量。化學誘導物必須購買、儲存、精準加入無菌容器，之後還要在產品流中被追蹤交代，而且是隨每一批次累加的經常成本。光不在迴路上多接一條管線、不在穿透液留下殘留，而且可以由軟體重新給劑量，不必有人打開容器——這正是天氣預報能夠驅動生產的原因：指令路徑終點是一顆 LED，不是一桶誘導物。關於對培養物的代價：六個光照組的生長速率介於每小時 0.279 到 0.317，全部落在一個標準誤差內，所以在這些強度下綠光誘導沒有可量測的生長代價。這張生長數據就是菌株標示有爭議的那一張，引用時只拿它談生長。",
