     "answer": "Because the reactor needs the protein outside the cell. B. subtilis is non-pathogenic and a natural secretor, so the permeate stream can carry protectant without a lysis step, and our whole build is the SubtiToolKit Golden Gate system, which is written for B. subtilis and Gram-positive hosts; the CcaS/CcaR optogenetics we took the circuit from is itself B. subtilis work. The secretion choice rests on exactly one piece of evidence: the 2 August fractionation blot, with ACC deaminase in the supernatant lanes and both pellet lanes blank, one blot with no loading control. We never built the circuit in E. coli, so we cannot compare yields.",
