     "id": "GT-17",
     "type": "decision",
     "q": "Why define success as a 27-criterion chain instead of showing that each component works?",
     "q_zh": "為什麼把成功定義為 27 條判準組成的一條鏈，而不是分別證明每個元件可以運作？",
     "answer": "Because components that each work do not make a system that works. Development's argument is that a failure in one link makes the success of the others insufficient, so for each of the six stages we asked five questions: what it must accomplish, what can be measured, what performance counts as success, what evidence is needed, and how the stage affects the rest. That produced 27 criteria with numbers attached, including detection accuracy at or above 90 per cent, CV at or below 10 per cent, detect-to-activate within 3 minutes, output retention at or above 80 per cent, transfer efficiency of at least 50 per cent as a starting proposal, and a 20 per cent plant improvement. The cost of writing it that way is a scoreboard with nothing Met, and two criteria we never defined at all.",
     "answer_zh": "因為各自可運作的元件並不等於可運作的系統。Development 頁的論點是：一環失效會讓其他環節的成功變得不足，所以我們對六個階段各問五個問題：它必須達成什麼、什麼可以被量化、什麼表現才算成功、需要什麼證據、這一階段如何影響其餘。這產生了 27 條附帶數字的判準，包括偵測準確度達 90% 以上、變異係數 10% 以下、偵測到啟動在 3 分鐘內、輸出維持率 80% 以上、作為初步提案的轉移效率至少 50%，以及植物表現改善 20%。這樣寫的代價是一張沒有任何一項達成的成績表，以及兩條我們根本沒定義的判準。",
