     "answer": "It stops short of the field and of certification. Taiwan's organic standards prohibit genetically modified preparations and microbial fertilisers must be free of GM microbes, which is why physical containment is the centre of the design and why farmers at our 5 September forum asked whether a treated crop could still be certified organic; our Laws and Regulations work does not conclude that it can. Nothing has run outside the bench: no field trial, no crop species, and the two delivery routes, hydroponic circulation and soil irrigation, exist as a design informed by the Yes Health iFarm visit rather than as a tested connection to real plumbing. Farmer Chen's willingness, quoted on the homepage, is an interview answer about a bench unit, not a deployment.",
